The intended SQL joins drugbank_transporters_polypeptides (tpp) to drugbank_transporters_polypeptides_pfams (tppf) via tppf.parent_key = tpp.id and filters by a specific transporter polypeptide ID (:polypeptide_id). The error 'Incorrect number of bindings supplied' occurred because the placeholder :polypeptide_id was not provided, so no rows could be returned. From the schema, drugbank_transporters_polypeptides_pfams has columns (identifier, name, parent_key), where parent_key stores the transporter polypeptide ID. Thus, supplying the polypeptide ID will yield the linked Pfam identifiers and names. A minimal working query is:
SELECT DISTINCT identifier, name FROM drugbank_transporters_polypeptides_pfams WHERE parent_key = :polypeptide_id ORDER BY identifier, name;
Based on table examples, ABC transporters commonly map to PF00005 (ABC_tran) and PF00664 (ABC_membrane) — consistent with the unstructured passages describing ABC transporters (e.g., TruMDR2, ABCG2) — but the exact set depends on the specific polypeptide ID you provide.

