The SQL failed because the required parameter :drugbank_id was not supplied ("Incorrect number of bindings supplied"). The Drugs.com URL is stored in drugbank_drug_external_links under url where resource='Drugs.com' and parent_key is the DrugBank ID. Once you provide the ID, use a bound parameter query such as:

SELECT url
FROM drugbank_drug_external_links
WHERE resource = 'Drugs.com' AND parent_key = ?;

If you don’t know the DrugBank ID but have a drug name, we can first resolve the ID via the synonyms table and then fetch the URL:

-- Find DrugBank ID by synonym/name
SELECT drugbank_id FROM drugbank_drug_syn WHERE LOWER(synonym) = LOWER(?);

-- Then get the Drugs.com link
SELECT url FROM drugbank_drug_external_links WHERE resource = 'Drugs.com' AND parent_key = ?;

Provide either the DrugBank ID or the drug name/synonym, and I’ll return the exact Drugs.com link.

